    "body": "I sometimes use ' and \" as suffix to numbers like _5'_ for _5 minutes_ or 10'' for _10 seconds_. It is already possible to achieve this with the mini.pairs configuration, like this:\r\n```\r\nlocal pairs_mappings = {\r\n    ['\"'] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = '\"\"', neigh_pattern = '[^%d\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\r\n    [\"'\"] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = \"''\", neigh_pattern = '[^%w\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\r\n}\r\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup({ mappings = pairs_mappings })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat is, I effectively added `%d` to the `neigh_pattern` for both cases. Maybe this helps others, too.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I sometimes use ' and \" as suffix to numbers like <em>5'</em> for <em>5 minutes</em> or 10'' for <em>10 seconds</em>. It is already possible to achieve this with the mini.pairs configuration, like this:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local pairs_mappings = {\n    ['&quot;'] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = '&quot;&quot;', neigh_pattern = '[^%d\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n    [&quot;'&quot;] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = &quot;''&quot;, neigh_pattern = '[^%w\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n}\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup({ mappings = pairs_mappings })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">local pairs_mappings = {\n    ['\"'] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = '\"\"', neigh_pattern = '[^%d\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n    [\"'\"] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = \"''\", neigh_pattern = '[^%w\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n}\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup({ mappings = pairs_mappings })\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">That is, I effectively added <code class=\"notranslate\">%d</code> to the <code class=\"notranslate\">neigh_pattern</code> for both cases. Maybe this helps others, too.</p>",
    "bodyText": "I sometimes use ' and \" as suffix to numbers like 5' for 5 minutes or 10'' for 10 seconds. It is already possible to achieve this with the mini.pairs configuration, like this:\nlocal pairs_mappings = {\n    ['\"'] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = '\"\"', neigh_pattern = '[^%d\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n    [\"'\"] = { action = 'closeopen', pair = \"''\", neigh_pattern = '[^%w\\\\].', register = { cr = false } },\n}\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup({ mappings = pairs_mappings })\n\nThat is, I effectively added %d to the neigh_pattern for both cases. Maybe this helps others, too.",
